  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c81fac6eb33b4658925a2b445371324b",
      "statement": "Tier-1 admission requires all four controls to pass simultaneously: DSR p-value at or above 0.90, PBO below 0.5, walk-forward OOS Sharpe above 0 with an OOS-to-IS ratio at or above 0.5 (plus CPCV positive fraction at or above 0.5 when computable), and a look-ahead audit that passes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/admission-criteria.md#L22-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4140904ba0baccdbbaafe6e0f51ba9ee6f648e056704609ec0fc8a675b55256c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5a19c6f29a2b417a98846cfc12bcd49a",
      "statement": "On the curated library num_trials is 1, so the expected best-of-N term is zero and DSR runs undeflated with no multiple-testing correction; the reason given is that there was no search of ours to charge for and promoting a strategy into a larger library must not retroactively move its score.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/admission-criteria.md#L38-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c3b9fcb7f7d98e8ee5419ae05ede4eacfe0e741904d2431b4683452bb983bc1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d4ef76a40bf14c3d82446f22cf9039e5",
      "statement": "The board-level selection bias a user incurs by picking the best of N displayed strategies is disclosed rather than corrected: the Benjamini-Hochberg helpers exist with zero non-test callers, so the gate must not be described as correcting selection bias across the library.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/admission-criteria.md#L38-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c3b9fcb7f7d98e8ee5419ae05ede4eacfe0e741904d2431b4683452bb983bc1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ca6f628e986d4dcc9be4389d97b7abd8",
      "statement": "PBO is a library-level property rather than a per-strategy score: one value is computed per analytics-engine run and attached to every strategy in it, and a value at or above 0.5 means the in-sample-optimal strategy is expected to underperform the out-of-sample median.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/admission-criteria.md#L72-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1880079f0ea22c8d8a36b6071bf994f6091a5ba32d906c4201b85e8f2f8f9822:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_10a8ad232ac34606ba85bbfdcdde3089",
      "statement": "The walk-forward check has two parts — an absolute floor that no negative out-of-sample Sharpe can pass, and a cliff check requiring the out-of-sample edge to retain at least half the in-sample edge — with the in-sample Sharpe computed on the first 70% slice only so the ratio cannot be inflated by leaking held-out data into the denominator.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/admission-criteria.md#L84-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4300843d9cba3e2f6528886523c4ba54d4402147440e24d6b700eabd7a12f758:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a96eea4f857d4c71be1c7c1228544a96",
      "statement": "The look-ahead audit must return zero warnings to pass, any flagged forward-data access blocks admission until a reviewer resolves it, and a strategy that cannot be parsed also fails because a SyntaxError returns passed=False rather than being skipped.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/quant/admission-criteria.md#L99-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3ad4afb9e583d384b7501d6cf9681a1bd08cf5b738bc945e14ac2a3de5c3976:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
